WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074

2
00:00:40.082 --> 00:00:41.004
<i>Magic trick.</i>

3
00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:54.263
You guys. That poor kid
might have really gotten hurt.

4
00:00:54.555 --> 00:00:56.728
Oh, sweetie. It's hilarious.

5
00:00:58.141 --> 00:01:00.644
Okay, we are late. I gotta go.

6
00:01:01.103 --> 00:01:02.730
Thanks for taking care of her, Dad.

7
00:01:03.146 --> 00:01:04.773
Bye, Rudie. I love you.

8
00:01:04.856 --> 00:01:06.199
Bye, Chickenbutt.

9
00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:09.156
Let's get one of us both.

10
00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:11.288
- Okay.
- Okay.

11
00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:18.037
<i>There's no place like Magic Land.</i>

12
00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.463
That looks fun.

13
00:01:20.872 --> 00:01:22.169
Of course, I can't go.

14
00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:26.796
It's all hype anyway. You make your own fun.

15
00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:31.349
Besides, amusement parks these days...

16
00:01:32.217 --> 00:01:35.642
Let's just say Magic Land
lost its magic a long time ago.

17
00:01:35.971 --> 00:01:38.315
<i>Or for the best deal, purchase a memb...</i>

18
00:01:38.682 --> 00:01:39.809
And I should know.

19
00:01:43.478 --> 00:01:45.400
Your mom ever tell you that your old papaw

20
00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.983
owned one of the greatest
amusement parks of all time?

21
00:01:50.068 --> 00:01:51.866
- She didn't?
- No.

22
00:01:52.362 --> 00:01:54.581
What? It was epic.

23
00:01:55.365 --> 00:01:56.958
That's my damn legacy.

24
00:01:58.035 --> 00:02:00.207
Yeah, this was when I was living

25
00:02:00.287 --> 00:02:02.540
up in the woods near Calico Ridge.

26
00:02:03.206 --> 00:02:04.549
<i>It was a wild time.</i>

27
00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:13.470
Things could be worse.

28
00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:16.014
<i>My next-door neighbor was an alcoholic bear</i>

29
00:02:16.094 --> 00:02:19.724
<i>who would sneak into my yard
and try to kill me for my beer.</i>

30
00:02:20.641 --> 00:02:22.484
<i>Yep, true story.</i>

31
00:02:22.684 --> 00:02:24.857
Go on. Go away.

32
00:02:25.771 --> 00:02:27.899
Go away. No, no. Come on.

33
00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:29.486
No, no. No, no.

34
00:02:29.566 --> 00:02:31.944
Don't be a prick. Don't you be a prick.

35
00:02:35.614 --> 00:02:38.493
<i>He was a persistent little bastard too.</i>

36
00:02:38.784 --> 00:02:40.581
<i>I would have shared the beer with him,</i>

37
00:02:40.661 --> 00:02:43.164
<i>but he was kind of an angry drunk.</i>

38
00:02:43.246 --> 00:02:45.044
No, no. Go, go.

39
00:02:45.749 --> 00:02:46.591
Good boy.

40
00:03:08.438 --> 00:03:09.530
Oh, fuck.

41
00:03:23.829 --> 00:03:25.081
Come on, Papaw.

42
00:03:25.706 --> 00:03:27.458
What? That's how it happened.

43
00:03:27.749 --> 00:03:29.046
Honest Injun.

44
00:03:31.002 --> 00:03:32.549
Guess you can't say that anymore.

45
00:03:34.506 --> 00:03:35.928
<i>Those days were different.</i>

46
00:03:36.383 --> 00:03:38.010
<i>There weren't so many rules.</i>

47
00:03:38.385 --> 00:03:41.058
<i>Kids were allowed just to be kids</i>

48
00:03:41.138 --> 00:03:42.765
<i>and do what kids love to do.</i>

49
00:03:44.141 --> 00:03:46.439
<i>Dumb, crazy shit they might regret.</i>

50
00:03:54.484 --> 00:03:56.452
<i>Action Point was my baby.</i>

51
00:03:56.695 --> 00:03:58.413
<i>I built her from the ground up.</i>

52
00:03:58.822 --> 00:04:00.243
<i>It wasn't some huge monster park,</i>

53
00:04:00.323 --> 00:04:02.496
<i>just a couple of slides and rides,</i>

54
00:04:02.576 --> 00:04:04.954
<i>but all the kids in town loved it.</i>

55
00:04:07.122 --> 00:04:10.295
<i>And the ones who had nowhere to go
and no one to look after 'em,</i>

56
00:04:10.375 --> 00:04:11.922
<i>well, I put 'em to work.</i>

57
00:04:12.377 --> 00:04:14.380
<i>I called them the Shitbirds.</i>

58
00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:17.466
<i>There was Ziffel. He was our chief engineer.</i>

59
00:04:18.508 --> 00:04:20.385
<i>Stiv worked security.</i>

60
00:04:21.595 --> 00:04:22.517
Don't fuck with me.

61
00:04:22.846 --> 00:04:25.224
<i>Four Finger Annie was our ride supervisor.</i>

62
00:04:26.391 --> 00:04:28.234
<i>Rodney, he was the numbers guy.</i>

63
00:04:29.436 --> 00:04:31.655
<i>Hot Headed Pete was in charge of complaining.</i>

64
00:04:32.147 --> 00:04:33.865
Can someone help me with this? Hello?

65
00:04:34.191 --> 00:04:35.738
<i>And then there was Killer.</i>

66
00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:39.825
<i>He wasn't exactly a kid
and he wasn't on the payroll,</i>

67
00:04:39.905 --> 00:04:41.368
<i>but he did come every day</i>

68
00:04:41.448 --> 00:04:43.451
<i>to pick fights with random strangers.</i>

69
00:04:44.075 --> 00:04:45.247
<i>Never a dull moment.</i>

70
00:04:45.827 --> 00:04:46.998
<i>To be honest,</i>

71
00:04:47.078 --> 00:04:49.422
<i>I think he escaped from a mental hospital.</i>

72
00:04:50.415 --> 00:04:51.257
<i>Anyhoo...</i>

73
00:04:51.666 --> 00:04:53.543
<i>The park bordered the Calico River,</i>

74
00:04:53.627 --> 00:04:55.630
<i>so we had water activities too.</i>

75
00:04:56.254 --> 00:04:58.973
<i>And your Great Uncle Benny
was in charge down there.</i>

76
00:04:59.382 --> 00:05:01.805
<i>Not one single person
ever drowned on his watch</i>

77
00:05:01.885 --> 00:05:02.977
<i>most of the time.</i>

78
00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:04.516
- And I looked up...
- Help!

79
00:05:04.596 --> 00:05:07.145
...and I saw her vagina
staring me right in the eye.

80
00:05:08.225 --> 00:05:11.148
And I knew, like,
"No, this is not just for peeing.

81
00:05:11.228 --> 00:05:12.525
This is for something else."

82
00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:15.486
Up until then I thought
babies came out of the butt.

83
00:05:16.358 --> 00:05:18.235
<i>Everyone loved to hear his stories,</i>

84
00:05:18.652 --> 00:05:20.404
<i>none of which I will share with you,
young lady.</i>

85
00:05:20.487 --> 00:05:21.329
Help me!

86
00:05:22.113 --> 00:05:26.288
<i>Back then there was a little thing
called personal responsibility.</i>

87
00:05:26.368 --> 00:05:28.211
<i>If you screwed up and got hurt,</i>

88
00:05:28.745 --> 00:05:31.460
<i>you didn't call no lawyer or the media.</i>

89
00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:33.167
<i>You just dusted yourself off</i>

90
00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:35.674
<i>and bragged about it
to your dumb little buddies.</i>

91
00:05:42.425 --> 00:05:44.348
That sounds awesome. What happened to it?

92
00:05:49.224 --> 00:05:51.568
Well, that's a long story.

93
00:05:52.185 --> 00:05:54.188
But we have all afternoon, right?

94
00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:57.865
Well, you're absolutely right.

95
00:05:58.358 --> 00:05:59.530
Hey, speaking of...

96
00:06:02.237 --> 00:06:03.955
Who wants a little mani-pedi?

97
00:06:04.406 --> 00:06:05.783
I mean, it's just us girls.

98
00:06:18.086 --> 00:06:19.713
Go, go, go!

99
00:06:20.088 --> 00:06:21.681
Lay off the brakes, asshole.

100
00:06:27.721 --> 00:06:28.688
Here, boss.

101
00:06:33.518 --> 00:06:35.020
Goddamn it, Lumpy.

102
00:06:35.103 --> 00:06:36.525
What were you trying to do?

103
00:06:36.938 --> 00:06:38.986
- I wanted to go faster.
- That's fair.

104
00:06:42.527 --> 00:06:43.494
Give me that tape.

105
00:06:45.113 --> 00:06:46.035
Just hold it.

106
00:06:47.741 --> 00:06:50.540
Give her the old criss-cross apple sauce.

107
00:06:52.829 --> 00:06:55.924
All right. That'll hold her for a bit, Merle.

108
00:06:58.668 --> 00:07:01.296
Now, let me take a look at that thing.

109
00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:07.636
Going to...

110
00:07:07.719 --> 00:07:08.641
There we go.

111
00:07:11.848 --> 00:07:14.437
What? That's what
it was invented for in Vietnam.

112
00:07:14.517 --> 00:07:16.360
Better than stitches, stronger than skin.

113
00:07:17.145 --> 00:07:17.987
You're gonna be all right.

114
00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:21.817
Where the hell's Rodney?

115
00:07:22.734 --> 00:07:23.576
Rodney!

116
00:07:28.031 --> 00:07:29.908
- You wanted to see me?
- Yeah.

117
00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:34.538
Something's off. I see our regular kids.

118
00:07:34.621 --> 00:07:37.545
But where's the fresh fish?
What's our attendance today?

119
00:07:38.416 --> 00:07:41.670
Down about 45%.
Pretty close to my projections.

120
00:07:41.753 --> 00:07:44.848
It could be worse,
considering 7 Parks just opened.

121
00:07:46.424 --> 00:07:48.513
The new amusement park
a half-hour's drive from here.

122
00:07:48.593 --> 00:07:50.971
I told you they were building it
all last winter.

123
00:07:51.846 --> 00:07:54.816
That's not my listening season.
You should have told me louder.

124
00:07:55.183 --> 00:07:58.483
You heard me. It's just that
selective proactivity of yours.

125
00:07:59.354 --> 00:08:00.355
Get lost, Rodney.

126
00:08:12.033 --> 00:08:13.160
Hello there.

127
00:08:13.827 --> 00:08:15.045
Any of you work here?

128
00:08:15.495 --> 00:08:16.838
Yeah, not if we can help it.

129
00:08:18.081 --> 00:08:18.957
I see.

130
00:08:20.083 --> 00:08:22.381
I'm Greg Knoblach
with Trustwood Developments.

131
00:08:22.961 --> 00:08:24.463
You've probably seen my billboards.

132
00:08:28.299 --> 00:08:30.518
Okay. I was looking for D.C.

133
00:08:31.386 --> 00:08:33.730
Well, lookee here. Old Knoblick.

134
00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:37.230
It's Knoblach, and that wasn't
even funny in high school.

135
00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:39.648
D.C., the chairlift broke again.

136
00:08:40.729 --> 00:08:42.447
- Oh, shit.
- Help me!

137
00:08:43.064 --> 00:08:44.191
Rodney!

138
00:08:45.233 --> 00:08:46.109
Amazing.

139
00:08:47.235 --> 00:08:48.612
Anyway, back to why I'm here.

140
00:08:48.903 --> 00:08:51.782
I suppose you probably heard
you got some competition in town now.

141
00:08:51.865 --> 00:08:54.204
Yeah, yeah, yeah, I know all about 7 Narcs.

142
00:08:54.284 --> 00:08:56.287
Yeah. Here, take a look at those, kids.

143
00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:59.542
They've got log flumes, roller coasters,

144
00:08:59.622 --> 00:09:01.465
and a chairlift that actually works.

145
00:09:03.126 --> 00:09:05.298
My son Travis just took a job there
for the summer.

146
00:09:05.378 --> 00:09:06.425
Little cocksucker.

147
00:09:06.963 --> 00:09:10.092
Looks like a big, bright,
shiny corporate asshole to me.

148
00:09:11.801 --> 00:09:13.053
Okay, listen, D.C.

149
00:09:14.971 --> 00:09:16.017
What's he got in here?

150
00:09:16.097 --> 00:09:17.599
I got friends at the bank.

151
00:09:17.807 --> 00:09:20.481
So I know you took out a loan
on this place last year.

152
00:09:21.644 --> 00:09:23.066
What was it, 100,000?

153
00:09:24.189 --> 00:09:26.066
How are you ever gonna pay that off?

154
00:09:27.192 --> 00:09:28.905
Let me find a buyer for your land.

155
00:09:28.985 --> 00:09:31.238
It's not gonna be easy,
but I'm sure I can find somebody.

156
00:09:32.947 --> 00:09:34.665
Well, look, Nodgecock.

157
00:09:35.492 --> 00:09:38.164
I didn't build this place
for you or the bank.

158
00:09:38.244 --> 00:09:39.587
I built it for the kids.

159
00:09:40.246 --> 00:09:43.625
So I'm not selling
to any of you fanny-blowers.

160
00:09:44.209 --> 00:09:45.051
Good day.

161
00:09:47.629 --> 00:09:48.847
Hey. Hey!

162
00:09:49.172 --> 00:09:51.846
Hey, those are Cubans. Give me that.

163
00:09:52.926 --> 00:09:53.768
Give me that.

164
00:09:55.303 --> 00:09:57.852
You're lucky we saved your people
in that war.

165
00:09:59.766 --> 00:10:03.111
<i>And that's about the time
your mom arrived for the summer.</i>

166
00:10:19.285 --> 00:10:21.207
- Chickenbutt! Hi.
- Hi!

167
00:10:21.287 --> 00:10:23.415
I'm so glad to see you.

168
00:10:25.166 --> 00:10:26.509
I recognize those.

169
00:10:29.087 --> 00:10:31.385
How's your mom? Still hate me?

170
00:10:31.798 --> 00:10:34.301
Still with that guy, the physical therapist?

171
00:10:34.717 --> 00:10:37.265
She doesn't hate you,
and you know he's a doctor.

172
00:10:37.345 --> 00:10:39.188
Yeah, that's what he says.

173
00:10:40.515 --> 00:10:41.858
All right, baby.

174
00:10:43.643 --> 00:10:44.986
Well, let's hit it.

175
00:10:49.315 --> 00:10:52.410
You remember this one? You used
to love it when you were a kid.

176
00:10:59.534 --> 00:11:00.831
Here.

177
00:11:02.537 --> 00:11:03.459
Listen to this.

178
00:11:10.378 --> 00:11:13.427
Beat's good, but the lead singer
sounds kind of harelipped.

179
00:11:14.257 --> 00:11:17.386
- They're called The Clash.
- The Clash.

180
00:11:17.677 --> 00:11:20.391
They're playing New York.
A lot of my friends are going.

181
00:11:20.471 --> 00:11:21.472
It's no big deal.

182
00:11:24.142 --> 00:11:25.439
They're actually all right.

183
00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:28.650
Hey, well, I think their tour's
coming through LA.

184
00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:30.983
You think maybe we could check 'em out?

185
00:11:31.733 --> 00:11:33.531
Sure. We got all summer.

186
00:11:39.324 --> 00:11:40.542
Home sweet home.

187
00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:45.122
House looks the same.

188
00:11:47.665 --> 00:11:49.338
Spent a little time cleaning her up.

189
00:11:51.544 --> 00:11:53.217
I got the luggage. Don't worry about it.

190
00:11:57.634 --> 00:11:58.510
<i>Draw.</i>

191
00:11:59.844 --> 00:12:01.062
<i>Too slow.</i>

192
00:12:03.556 --> 00:12:06.146
- Boogie!
- Benny! Oh, my God!

193
00:12:06.226 --> 00:12:08.695
The hell you doing here?
You're supposed to be at the lagoon.

194
00:12:12.023 --> 00:12:14.526
I don't believe it. You blossomed.

195
00:12:18.321 --> 00:12:19.664
I'm gonna go unpack.

196
00:12:20.073 --> 00:12:22.451
- You gotta see my new hatchet.
- Oh, Jesus.

197
00:12:22.533 --> 00:12:24.456
I invented this game.
It's called Kill the White Man.

198
00:12:24.911 --> 00:12:26.333
You think this shirt makes me look fat?

199
00:12:26.788 --> 00:12:28.381
I don't really care if it does. It's rad.

200
00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:30.292
I stole it from my sister.

201
00:12:38.758 --> 00:12:40.722
Oh, please, Dad. It's a tampon.

202
00:12:40.802 --> 00:12:42.554
Do not swear at me, young lady.

203
00:12:43.263 --> 00:12:44.936
It's fine. It's totally natural.

204
00:12:45.515 --> 00:12:48.735
She left Action Point a child.
She returned a woman.

205
00:12:49.102 --> 00:12:51.025
All right, that's it. Back to the lagoon.

206
00:12:52.146 --> 00:12:53.568
Come by and see me later, Boogie.

207
00:12:54.065 --> 00:12:55.692
We'll gab like little schoolgirls.

208
00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:57.743
- Okay, Benny.
- Bye.

209
00:12:58.861 --> 00:12:59.988
He's a peach.

210
00:13:00.697 --> 00:13:02.950
Oh, God. I'm gonna go. Are you okay?

211
00:13:04.993 --> 00:13:06.916
Actually... Well, no. No, it can wait.

212
00:13:07.453 --> 00:13:09.292
- You sure?
- Yeah. I'm gonna get a shower.

213
00:13:09.372 --> 00:13:11.249
I'll come find you later. We can talk then.

214
00:13:11.332 --> 00:13:12.174
Okay.

215
00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:16.929
We got a rogue bear around here,
so keep an eye out.

216
00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:19.884
There's some bear repellent
over next to the hairspray.

217
00:13:20.383 --> 00:13:22.135
But don't get 'em mixed up.

218
00:13:22.218 --> 00:13:23.219
<i>Draw.</i>

219
00:13:24.137 --> 00:13:25.355
<i>Too slow.</i>

220
00:13:25.888 --> 00:13:27.435
<i>Sounds like my mom's worst nightmare.</i>

221
00:13:27.890 --> 00:13:29.392
Well, it wasn't back then.

222
00:13:29.726 --> 00:13:31.353
She wasn't the uptight...

223
00:13:32.061 --> 00:13:33.859
excellent mother she is now.

224
00:13:34.063 --> 00:13:35.861
She was pretty normal.

225
00:13:38.109 --> 00:13:39.948
Come on, I was gonna paint your nails.

226
00:13:40.028 --> 00:13:41.324
- You don't wanna...
- Papaw.

227
00:13:41.404 --> 00:13:42.280
You...

228
00:13:43.114 --> 00:13:44.957
Okay. Suit yourself.

229
00:13:53.166 --> 00:13:55.920
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.
My tootsies are ticklish.

230
00:13:58.212 --> 00:13:59.304
No!

231
00:14:00.965 --> 00:14:01.807
You touched 'em.

232
00:14:03.009 --> 00:14:05.103
It looks good. It's an improvement.

233
00:14:15.521 --> 00:14:17.398
- Smartass.
- All right, let's do this.

234
00:14:18.024 --> 00:14:20.027
Boogie, it's on you.

235
00:14:23.154 --> 00:14:24.155
You ready, Stiv?

236
00:14:25.406 --> 00:14:26.453
Okay.

237
00:14:28.034 --> 00:14:30.458
Three, two, one!

238
00:14:33.081 --> 00:14:33.957
It works!

239
00:14:35.083 --> 00:14:36.335
Sorry, Stiv!

240
00:14:37.126 --> 00:14:38.469
She's not sorry.

241
00:14:39.295 --> 00:14:40.467
Hey, D.C.

242
00:14:41.798 --> 00:14:43.175
Relax, Pete.

243
00:14:43.466 --> 00:14:46.720
It's not gonna hurt you. Just a baby snake.

244
00:14:47.011 --> 00:14:49.514
- Oh, my God.
- Found him out in the woodpile.

245
00:14:49.722 --> 00:14:51.816
What do you think, D.C.? Can I keep him?

246
00:14:52.183 --> 00:14:54.937
Sure, Killer.
Just get him the hell out of here.

247
00:14:55.269 --> 00:14:56.482
Awesome.

248
00:14:56.562 --> 00:14:58.064
Hey, D.C., not so awesome

249
00:14:58.147 --> 00:15:02.118
is that snake came from underneath
the last piece of lumber we got.

250
00:15:02.944 --> 00:15:05.743
Damn. We need that wood for the rides.

251
00:15:06.322 --> 00:15:08.040
How we looking on funds, Rodney?

